    <us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCovenantDescription contextRef="c-147" id="f-908">The Term Loan Agreement requires us to maintain, on a consolidated basis, a net leverage ratio of total net indebtedness to adjusted EBITDA, as defined in the Term Loan Agreement and calculated as of the last day of each fiscal quarter, not to exceed 3.25 to 1.00, subject to a temporary four fiscal quarter increase in such maximum ratio to 3.75 to 1.00 following certain material acquisitions. Our obligations under the Term Loan Agreement are unsecured.</us-gaap:DebtInstrumentCovenantDescription>
    <mu:DebtInstrumentCovenantRatioOfNetDebtToAdjustedEBITDA contextRef="c-150" decimals="INF" id="f-909" unitRef="rate">3.25</mu:DebtInstrumentCovenantRatioOfNetDebtToAdjustedEBITDA>
    <mu:DebtInstrumentCovenantRatioOfNetDebtToAdjustedEBITDATemporaryIncrease contextRef="c-150" decimals="INF" id="f-910" unitRef="rate">3.75</mu:DebtInstrumentCovenantRatioOfNetDebtToAdjustedEBITDATemporaryIncrease>
